<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Venetian Dalmatia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1420">1420</a>–<a href="/years/1797">1797</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Venetian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dalmatia">Dalmatia</a> was the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a>'s possession on the eastern Adriatic coast, held from 1420, when Venice bought the Hungarian claim and took over most coastal towns, until the fall of the republic in 1797. Governed from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zadar">Zadar</a>, it supplied sailors, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timber">timber</a> and soldiers. The wars with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> extended it inland in the late 17th and early 18th centuries; it then passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/venetian-dalmatia.jpg" alt="Venetian Dalmatia" width="320" height="227" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Maximilian Dörrbecker (Chumwa) · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Venezianische_Kolonien.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
